1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,688
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:30,196
[Helena] <i>You know,</i>
<i>when your phone blacks out,</i>

6
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,657
<i>it means it's been cloned.</i>

7
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,200
<i>-That's impossible, Madam.</i>
<i>-Shut up!</i>

8
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:36,911
[Lily] <i>I'm sure Red Dragon already knows</i>

9
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:38,371
<i>that I'm her enemy.</i>

10
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:41,082
[Arnaldo] <i>I've been having some</i>
<i>thoughts lately. About a woman.</i>

11
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:43,501
<i>-Well, what do you see?</i>
<i>-Lustful things towards her.</i>

12
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:44,961
<i>Where did you get this, by the way?</i>

13
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:46,796
<i>I found it inside the Bible</i>
<i>Grandpa gave me.</i>

14
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,549
<i>Madam, we've traced the IMEI number</i>
<i>of whoever tapped Mercedes' phone.</i>

15
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:52,927
<i>She was right. The one</i>
<i>behind all this is Lily Cruz.</i>

16
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:56,222
<i>I missed you, so I was thinking… lunch?</i>

17
00:00:56,306 --> 00:01:00,310
<i>I was just thinking</i>
<i>of the exact same thing.</i>

18
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:01,895
[Julio] <i>Why are you furious?</i>

19
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:09,736
<i>Is it because Arnaldo is slowly</i>
<i>starting to remember Ivy Aguas?</i>

20
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:13,573
[Diego] <i>Ivy Aguas is dead.</i>
<i>Both she and the old Arnaldo!</i>

21
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:18,328
<i>I want you to kill Diego Torillo now!</i>

22
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:22,040
[Lily] <i>I'm done playing pretend,</i>
<i>Helena Montoya.</i>

23
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:26,294
<i>So now, I'm going to make sure</i>
<i>you admit it yourself.</i>

24
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:28,713
<i>That you are none other than Red Dragon.</i>

25
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:30,673
[Diego] <i>Nanny, don't tell</i>
<i>Uncle Pandoy, okay?</i>

26
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:32,425
<i>I bought him his favorite cake.</i>

27
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:35,470
[Ivy] <i>Wow, Mama. The fish tastes amazing.</i>

28
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:36,846
<i>It's not fish.</i>

29
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,640
<i>It's snake.</i>

30
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:44,020
[Helena] <i>I made it.</i>

31
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:49,275
Emilia told me you have
a fondness for snakes.

32
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,028
[Lily chuckling]

33
00:01:54,489 --> 00:01:55,949
Of course, Emilia.

34
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,412
By the way, I'm curious.

35
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:05,208
Were you born in the year of the snake?

36
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:07,669
[tense music playing]

37
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:10,505
No.

38
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:11,965
No, Mama.

39
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:14,300
I think

40
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:16,052
it was the year of the dog.

41
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,971
And, you know, I read something.

42
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:20,682
I hope you weren't born
in the year of the dragon,

43
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:22,559
because dragons and dogs

44
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:24,978
are mortal enemies.

45
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:28,273
[tense music swells]

46
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:32,068
[chuckling]

47
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:36,573
I really wouldn't know because
I don't follow these things.

48
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:42,912
<i>But you know what? Speaking of dogs.</i>

49
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:45,498
I don't really like them

50
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:49,544
because they are so needy

51
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:52,505
and manipulative.

52
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:57,802
You know, they play nice and cute,

53
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:01,306
but when you turn around, they bite you.

54
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:02,599
[chuckles]

55
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:04,309
Yes, Mama.

56
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:07,061
Yes! It's true.

57
00:03:07,145 --> 00:03:08,980
That's what dogs are like.

58
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:12,400
But, at least, they're loyal.

59
00:03:13,026 --> 00:03:17,947
Like, when someone thinks
to hurt their loved ones,

60
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:19,699
that's when they attack.

61
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:25,204
I still think they're pathetic creatures.

62
00:03:28,499 --> 00:03:30,501
[tense music playing]

63
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:36,424
[Jose] Hmm.

64
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,511
You know, you're a good cook.

65
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:42,388
[Jose scoffs]

66
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:44,432
[suspenseful music playing]

67
00:03:44,515 --> 00:03:45,725
Poor Diego.

68
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,020
He'll be surprised when he comes back.

69
00:03:51,564 --> 00:03:53,316
What do you want from us?

70
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:56,236
What do you want?!

71
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:57,278
Shh.

72
00:03:57,779 --> 00:03:59,405
Let us go!

73
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:01,157
-We didn't do any--
-Shut up!

74
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:03,534
[Loring exclaims, cries]

75
00:04:03,785 --> 00:04:04,786
Shut up!

76
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:10,083
[breathes heavily]

77
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:11,793
[suspenseful music playing]

78
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:13,586
[Pandoy sighs deeply]

79
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:18,424
[suspenseful music intensifies]

80
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:22,804
[phone ringing]

81
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:28,017
-Sanggano?
-Sir.

82
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:29,602
[Jose] We're all set.

83
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:32,230
We're just waiting for Diego.

84
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:35,942
Good.

85
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:37,402
And don't forget…

86
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:41,114
to bring his corpse to me.

87
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:43,199
Yes, sir.

88
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:48,705
[stutters] Diego?

89
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:50,832
-What will you do to Diego?
-Diego.

90
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:54,460
We already did what you want.
Isn't that enough?!

91
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:56,629
[Loring cries] Don't kill Diego!

92
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:58,631
Not him, please! No… Not Diego.

93
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:01,092
-What did I tell you? What did I tell you?
-Not Diego, please.

94
00:05:01,175 --> 00:05:02,635
-I told you to shut up!
-[Loring screams]

95
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,595
-[Jose] Well?
-We're begging you!

96
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:07,515
-Hey, you two.
-Not Diego!

97
00:05:07,598 --> 00:05:09,517
Keep an eye on these two here.

98
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:12,729
-[man] Yes, boss.
-I'll take care of Diego.

99
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:15,940
-Not Diego!
-Don't! Please, not Diego!

100
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:17,191
-Sanggano!
-We'll take care of them.

101
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:19,152
-Sanggano!
-Sit!

102
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:20,111
-Son.
-I said sit!

103
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:21,237
-Sanggano!
-Sit down!

104
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:23,656
Sit down, or I'll use this gun on you!

105
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:26,784
-[Loring] Pandoy.
-Sit down.

106
00:05:27,952 --> 00:05:29,245
And shut up.

107
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:31,706
Diego.

108
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:33,833
Oh!

109
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:37,045
By the way, I hope you don't mind.

110
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:40,339
But you have to refrain
from calling me "Mama."

111
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:45,511
<i>Emilia's getting a little jealous.</i>

112
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:47,055
Got you.

113
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:50,475
-[upbeat music playing]
-[Lily laughs]

114
00:05:50,975 --> 00:05:53,311
Oh, Emilia! What's new?

115
00:05:53,936 --> 00:05:55,772
That's nothing new, Mama--

116
00:05:55,855 --> 00:05:57,774
I mean, Helena. That's nothing new.

117
00:05:57,857 --> 00:06:00,651
Your daughter has always been so insecure.

118
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:04,572
<i>Well, okay.</i>

119
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:07,241
So, I guess I'll just call you
by your first name.

120
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,952
Yeah, sure. Just call me "Helena."

121
00:06:10,036 --> 00:06:11,037
No.

122
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:14,123
No. Helena is too long.

123
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,462
Can I just call you…

124
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:20,296
"Hel"?

125
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:22,381
[tense music playing]

126
00:06:33,851 --> 00:06:37,396
[laughs]

127
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,273
That's so funny.

128
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:43,111
[Helena] <i>Oh!</i>

129
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:46,656
I almost forgot.
I have something to show you.

130
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:49,117
It'll just be a while.
I hope you don't mind.

131
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:51,160
Yeah, no problem.

132
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:54,497
[tense music continues playing]

133
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:25,319
I guess the boss took a long walk.

134
00:07:26,404 --> 00:07:27,989
It'll probably take him a while.

135
00:07:28,072 --> 00:07:29,449
Do you want to smoke?

136
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:31,242
What about these two?

137
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:33,035
Don't worry about them.

138
00:07:34,036 --> 00:07:36,539
They're too terrified to run away.

139
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:39,083
Let's go before the boss comes back.

140
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,461
[man 2] Just stay there.
Don't even try to escape!

141
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:43,713
Or else you'll both get it.

142
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,009
[Pandoy coughs]

143
00:07:52,346 --> 00:07:54,265
-Pandoy!
-Don't be so loud! Please!

144
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:55,099
Here.

145
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:57,518
What are you-- What should we--Huh?

146
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:59,520
-Pandoy.
-Wait? Wait. Ouch.

147
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:02,857
-Okay. Okay…
-We need to…

148
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,026
-My goodness.
-Hang in there!

149
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:06,944
[Pandoy] Hang in there.

150
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:10,031
-[Pandoy breathing heavily]
-[both struggling]

151
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:12,200
-There. It's done.
-[Loring groans]

152
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:14,911
[Loring groaning, crying]

153
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:19,290
Come on, come on! This way.

154
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:23,961
[suspenseful music playing]

155
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:27,173
[Julio chuckling]

156
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:31,219
Mister Goody Goody Gumdrops!

157
00:08:32,136 --> 00:08:34,722
It's only a matter of time, grandson.

158
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:38,768
The black sheep will soon be sheared.

159
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:43,814
[suspenseful music continues]

160
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,369
-[Pandoy panting] Come on…
-[Loring crying]

161
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:59,872
-Pandoy.
-Loring. Loring.

162
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:04,835
-[Loring sobs]
-Loring, let's go. Come on.

163
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,008
Diego!

164
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,301
Diego!

165
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:13,970
-Diego! Diego!
-Nanny! Uncle!

166
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:15,680
-Diego!
-[gunshots]

167
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:19,058
Loring! Run, Loring! Run!

168
00:09:19,141 --> 00:09:21,894
-Hey!
-Run! Run, Loring!

169
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:23,062
[gunshots]

170
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:25,439
-Pandoy! Pandoy!
-Uncle!

171
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:31,737
[Loring] Pandoy! Pandoy!

172
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:35,032
Pandoy! Pandoy!

173
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:35,908
[gunshot]

174
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:37,410
-[Loring shrieks]
-[Diego] No!

175
00:09:37,493 --> 00:09:39,579
-[Diego] No! No, no!
-[suspenseful music playing]

176
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:41,872
-[Diego] No! No! No!
-[Loring wailing]

177
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:43,457
-[gunshot]
-[Loring shrieks]

178
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:46,210
You bastard!

179
00:09:47,503 --> 00:09:49,463
[thuds]

180
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:02,560
Get over here! Bastard!

181
00:10:05,229 --> 00:10:06,063
[grunting]

182
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:08,190
[Diego grunts]

183
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:11,444
-He's mine!
-[man] Stop resisting!

184
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:13,321
[screaming]

185
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:14,697
You bastard!

186
00:10:16,949 --> 00:10:18,868
[Diego screams] You monster!

187
00:10:19,368 --> 00:10:21,829
[Diego groaning]

188
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:23,623
[Diego] Bastard!

189
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,918
[thuds]

190
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:30,504
-Give me your gun.
-[man 3] Mr. Diego!

191
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:32,173
-Give me your gun!
-[man 3] Mr. Diego!

192
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:33,424
People are coming.

193
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:34,717
Boss, we have to leave!

194
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:36,719
-They're coming.
-Let's go, boss.

195
00:10:36,802 --> 00:10:37,678
[grunts]

196
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,221
[man 1] They'll catch us here. Let's go.

197
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:44,644
[Diego groans]

198
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:47,647
[Diego groans]

199
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,110
[car engine starts]

200
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,279
[car doors close]

201
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,157
Nanny. Uncle.

202
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,910
-[breathing raggedly]
-[unsettling music playing]

203
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:04,955
[Diego grunts]

204
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:07,124
[Diego breathing raggedly]

205
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:09,877
Help.

206
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:11,504
Help.

207
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:12,838
Help us!

208
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:17,343
Nanny. Uncle.

209
00:11:17,426 --> 00:11:19,095
Nanny. Nanny!

210
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:21,764
[melancholic music playing]

211
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:26,894
Nanny.

212
00:11:26,977 --> 00:11:29,105
Nanny. Nanny! Nanny.

213
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:30,940
Uncle.

214
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,650
Uncle.

215
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:34,735
Nanny!

216
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:39,240
[melancholic music playing]

217
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,877
[Diego screaming]

218
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:56,382
Help!

219
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:59,009
Please help us!

220
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:03,639
Nanny. Nanny, please. Don't leave me.

221
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:04,849
Uncle!

222
00:12:04,932 --> 00:12:06,267
Help!

223
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:07,643
Help us!

224
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:11,772
Someone, please!

225
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:14,567
Help!

226
00:12:14,650 --> 00:12:15,901
Nanny!

227
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:16,986
[man] Mr. Diego!

228
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:18,737
[women crying]

229
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:20,197
Nanny. Nanny.

230
00:12:20,281 --> 00:12:24,368
Nanny. Uncle, hang in there.
Nanny. Uncle. Nanny.

231
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:26,203
-[women crying]
-[woman] Loring.

232
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:28,581
[women crying]

233
00:12:28,664 --> 00:12:30,499
Mr. Pandoy! Miss Loring!

234
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:33,294
-Help. Please help.
-Help us!

235
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:36,338
Let's bring them to the hospital! Hurry!

236
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:37,923
Mr. Pandoy!

237
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,341
Hurry. Let's bring them to the hospital.

238
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:43,179
[overlapping conversations]

239
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:44,680
[woman] Miss Loring!

240
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:47,975
[women crying]

241
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:52,563
[melancholic music playing]

242
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:12,958
[suspenseful music playing]

243
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:43,697
You really are a filthy dog.

244
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:49,578
<i>I turn my back for one second</i>

245
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:52,373
and off you go rummaging through my house?

246
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:55,292
Go, Mama. Go!

247
00:14:05,177 --> 00:14:06,762
A change in costume

248
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:09,765
and hairstyle too.

249
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:11,976
Are you going to a party?

250
00:14:13,978 --> 00:14:16,105
I have nothing to hide from you now.

251
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:18,566
That's right.

252
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:22,236
Because I know you bombed my properties!

253
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:24,238
And you sabotaged my shipment.

254
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:27,908
An eye for an eye, Red Dragon.

255
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:31,453
[tense music]

256
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:38,127
They say…

257
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:44,133
you're indestructible.

258
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:46,135
[Helena chuckling]

259
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:50,472
Let's see…

260
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:54,351
if you don't melt from my fire.

261
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:58,480
[dramatic music]

262
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:04,320
[Helena struggling]

263
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:06,614
Try me.

264
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:08,949
[Helena groans]

265
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:10,701
[Helena groans]

266
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:14,413
[Helena groaning]

267
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:17,625
[Helena groaning]

268
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,752
[tense music playing]

269
00:15:19,835 --> 00:15:20,836
[Helena gasps]

270
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,589
-Well? Aww!
-[Helena panting]

271
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:25,633
[Lily] What's this?

272
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:29,136
Is the Red Dragon shivering in fear?

273
00:15:29,219 --> 00:15:30,512
[dramatic music]

274
00:15:32,556 --> 00:15:34,016
[breathes heavily]

275
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:36,060
Why?

276
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:39,688
Are all those needles deadly?

277
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,024
Are they poisonous?

278
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:43,359
Huh?

279
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:45,945
-[Helena grunts]
-If that's the case,

280
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:47,905
then this is farewell.

281
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:52,451
Goodbye, Helena-Montoya-slash-Red-Dragon!

282
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,078
[Helena screams]

283
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:55,204
Ma.

284
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:57,331
[whimpers]

285
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:59,124
[suspenseful music]

286
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:01,543
[Lily] Hmm!

287
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:04,296
[laughing]

288
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:08,342
Why so scared, Red Dragon?

289
00:16:08,425 --> 00:16:12,429
Do you think I'd kill you with needles?

290
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:13,889
No!

291
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,599
You know what you deserve?

292
00:16:16,266 --> 00:16:17,226
Hmm?!

293
00:16:17,309 --> 00:16:18,811
What you deserve is

294
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:22,648
a slow death that eats at your soul.

295
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:26,902
You deserve to feel every ounce of pain!

296
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:32,116
You'll suffer so bad and so much

297
00:16:32,199 --> 00:16:35,202
that you'll long for death, instead!

298
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:38,789
[suspenseful music playing]

299
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:40,207
[Helena gasps]

300
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:44,545
[suspenseful music playing]

301
00:16:50,718 --> 00:16:51,719
Goodbye, Hel.

302
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:02,229
[screaming]

303
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:13,949
I would've killed that dragon
if I didn't have principles.

304
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:17,828
I would've pierced those needles
straight through her neck.

305
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:21,498
But then, we both know
how that woman is above the law.

306
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:24,126
She's even worse than the Ardientes…

307
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:28,756
which means I'll have
to resort to violence.

308
00:17:29,673 --> 00:17:31,759
Lily, it won't be that easy.

309
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:33,761
She's a wolf in sheep's clothing.

310
00:17:35,012 --> 00:17:36,013
Well, Mom,

311
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:38,057
she made an enemy out of me,

312
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:39,516
so I'm going to expose her.

313
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:42,895
I'm going to expose
all her crimes to the world.

314
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:45,314
[upbeat music]

315
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:51,779
[Helena] You think you can terrify me?!

316
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:55,783
I am Red Dragon…

317
00:17:56,950 --> 00:18:00,204
and I will kill you, Lily Cruz!

318
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:05,417
Prepare to die burning!

319
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:16,220
[laughing maniacally]

320
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:24,311
[groans]

321
00:18:29,441 --> 00:18:32,945
[groaning]

322
00:18:49,002 --> 00:18:51,088
No. No, no, no, Helena!

323
00:18:51,922 --> 00:18:52,923
No!

324
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:56,176
There's no reason to fear Lily Cruz.

325
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:02,432
You are Red Dragon!

326
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:08,689
You are going to drag that woman to hell!

327
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:15,320
Mercedes!

328
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:17,322
What's going on here?!

329
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:19,408
Can you please let me in?
I need to speak to my mother

330
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:22,744
because I'm going to help her
shred Lily Cruz into pieces!

331
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:23,787
So, let me in!

332
00:19:24,663 --> 00:19:26,415
Red Dragon can't see you right now.

333
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:27,749
Excuse me.

334
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:30,836
And, I meant that literally
because I have to go.

335
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:32,963
Hey! What's happening?!

336
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:36,550
Red Dragon is fine. She wants to be alone.

337
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:37,759
Oh, yeah right.

338
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:40,429
And who are you to tell me what to do?

339
00:19:40,804 --> 00:19:41,889
For the nth time,

340
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:45,017
Red Dragon doesn't want you
to know her location.

341
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:47,352
So, please, silence.

342
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:51,106
[scoffs] Silence? Why?
And who are you again?

343
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:53,442
You're just Mama's sidekick. A servant.

344
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:55,903
And, let me remind you, I'm her daughter.

345
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,029
So, let me in!

346
00:20:05,412 --> 00:20:06,413
[Jose] Governor.

347
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:08,790
[Julio chuckles]

348
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:13,879
-Sanggano.
-Governor.

349
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,423
You imbecile!

350
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:17,633
-Governor, please, stop!
-Please, stop!

351
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:18,550
Governor.

352
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:19,968
Let go of me!

353
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:22,512
Just look at yourself.

354
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:24,640
You're as purple as an eggplant!

355
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:27,017
You look like a bruised fruit!

356
00:20:27,309 --> 00:20:30,229
There's no doubt in my mind
that you failed!

357
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:35,943
Maybe it'd be better
if I buried you instead,

358
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:38,195
so I can put an end to all my problems!

359
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:40,280
But Governor…

360
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,199
I was able to kill his foster parents.

361
00:20:42,532 --> 00:20:44,534
-So what?!
-Governor, stop it, please.

362
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:47,412
Stop acting so smug. Are you deaf?

363
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:51,375
I told you to kill Diego Torillo!

364
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,712
Not his useless,
old peasant foster parents!

365
00:20:55,963 --> 00:21:00,175
Diego's the one
who's ruining all my plans!

366
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,887
I couldn't care less about those two!

367
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:06,807
Looks like they're all you can handle.

368
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:11,019
Hey, you. Go clean yourself up.

369
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:13,146
You're a disgrace!

370
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:14,815
Now, I don't care…

371
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:17,484
if you go blind.

372
00:21:18,819 --> 00:21:21,905
Or deaf. Or even if
you lose an arm or a leg.

373
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:28,078
Because I'm not letting you die
until you finish the job

374
00:21:28,161 --> 00:21:29,454
I asked you to do!

375
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,665
Now, get out!

376
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:34,042
You reek of defeat.

377
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,086
Scram! Go fix yourself.

378
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:38,005
Leave, all of you!

379
00:21:41,174 --> 00:21:42,801
What a bunch of idiots!

380
00:21:43,927 --> 00:21:46,305
[scoffs] Some colonel he is.

381
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:49,683
He's nothing but a useless bastard.

382
00:21:53,353 --> 00:21:54,187
[Diego] Nanny.

383
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:57,399
-[doctor] Ambu bag.
-Hang in there.

384
00:21:57,482 --> 00:21:58,859
-Sir. Sir.
-Wait.

385
00:21:58,942 --> 00:22:00,610
Wait, I'm not leaving.

386
00:22:00,902 --> 00:22:02,237
-We'll do everything we can.
-Nanny.

387
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:04,031
Please wait outside, Mr. Torillo.

388
00:22:04,114 --> 00:22:05,365
Nanny. No, I'm not leaving.

389
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:07,534
-Sir. Sir, sir.
-Diego. Diego.

390
00:22:07,617 --> 00:22:08,618
Mr. Torillo.

391
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:11,163
-Doc!
-We'll do everything--

392
00:22:11,246 --> 00:22:12,706
Doc, please do everything you can.

393
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:13,874
-Yes, sir. Yes, sir.
-Please, doc.

394
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:15,250
-Please wait outside.
-We trust you, doc.

395
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,338
[doctor] Continue CPR. Insert IV line.

396
00:22:19,421 --> 00:22:23,133
[somber music playing]

397
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,978
<i>Nanny Loring, Uncle Pandoy…</i>

398
00:22:36,938 --> 00:22:38,648
<i>we still have so many dreams.</i>

399
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,360
<i>You can't go yet.</i>

400
00:22:49,117 --> 00:22:52,079
[somber music continues playing]

401
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:11,681
[Jepoy] Lily? Lily?

402
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:14,267
-Aunt Camia, where's she?
-Jepoy.

403
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:16,228
[Lily] Jepoy, what is it?

404
00:23:16,311 --> 00:23:17,813
Did something happen?

405
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:20,357
Mr. Pandoy and Miss Loring…

406
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,399
they're in the hospital!

407
00:23:22,067 --> 00:23:24,569
In the hospital? Why? What happened?

408
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:27,864
Sanggano shot them.

409
00:23:27,948 --> 00:23:29,950
[gasping]

410
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:36,581
Those vile Ardientes.
I just know they're behind this.

411
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:38,750
Sanggano is one of their men.

412
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:42,462
What they did is just unforgivable.

413
00:23:43,213 --> 00:23:45,132
Loring and Pandoy never did
anything to the Ardientes.

414
00:23:46,466 --> 00:23:47,509
Mom, I need to see Diego.

415
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:50,345
I'm sure he's feeling twice
the pain that we are now.

416
00:23:50,428 --> 00:23:53,181
I need to see him.
I need to be there for him.

417
00:23:53,723 --> 00:23:55,851
-Is the car ready?
-I'll start it up.

418
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:59,146
[somber music playing]

419
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:04,192
[doctor] Sir.

420
00:24:04,693 --> 00:24:05,652
I'm so sorry.

421
00:24:06,319 --> 00:24:10,031
We did everything we could,
but they'd both lost too much blood.

422
00:24:10,657 --> 00:24:12,159
-No, no, no, no.
-I'm sorry, sir.

423
00:24:13,034 --> 00:24:15,120
-No, no, no, no.
-Sorry--

424
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:17,539
Nanny! Nanny.

425
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:21,459
[somber music continues]

426
00:24:22,752 --> 00:24:23,753
Nanny.

427
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:36,308
[weeping]

428
00:24:38,393 --> 00:24:40,437
[sobbing] My Nanny…

429
00:24:43,273 --> 00:24:44,274
Nanny.

430
00:24:49,279 --> 00:24:51,281
Nanny, I love you very much.

431
00:24:52,574 --> 00:24:58,038
[somber music continues]

432
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:24,898
Uncle.

433
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:28,652
Uncle.

434
00:25:34,157 --> 00:25:35,951
Uncle, I love you so much.

435
00:25:41,998 --> 00:25:43,416
Uncle, you can rest now.

436
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:51,716
[bleak music playing]

437
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:03,061
<i>Come here, Diego.</i>

438
00:26:03,853 --> 00:26:05,522
[Pandoy] <i>We're sorry</i>
<i>about what happened earlier.</i>

439
00:26:05,605 --> 00:26:07,274
[Diego] <i>I should be the one apologizing.</i>

440
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:10,485
[Loring] <i>It's a birthday party, right?</i>

441
00:26:10,568 --> 00:26:11,861
<i>Enough with the drama.</i>

442
00:26:12,195 --> 00:26:13,363
-[Pandoy laughs]
-[Loring] <i>We should be happy.</i>

443
00:26:13,446 --> 00:26:15,490
[Diego] <i>Well, I know</i>
<i>I wasn't being dramatic.</i>

444
00:26:17,617 --> 00:26:21,913
[dramatic music playing]

445
00:26:22,497 --> 00:26:27,961
-[fist thumping]
-[breathing raggedly]

446
00:26:35,051 --> 00:26:36,052
[gunshots]

447
00:26:36,136 --> 00:26:38,054
[Loring] <i>Pandoy! Pandoy!</i>

448
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:39,514
[Loring shrieks]

449
00:26:39,597 --> 00:26:40,724
[gunshots]

450
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:44,686
[dramatic music continues]

451
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:53,611
They'll pay for this.

452
00:26:54,904 --> 00:26:56,114
They'll pay for this!

453
00:26:59,951 --> 00:27:02,120
[Emilia] Stop it! Let go of me!

454
00:27:02,203 --> 00:27:05,623
You can't kick me out because
this is my mother's house!

455
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:07,667
And you! This isn't over, Mercedes!

456
00:27:08,043 --> 00:27:10,587
Let go of me! Let go of me!

457
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:13,131
This isn't over, Mercedes!

458
00:27:14,591 --> 00:27:16,009
[Emilia groans]

459
00:27:16,092 --> 00:27:17,802
[tense music playing]

460
00:27:20,055 --> 00:27:21,181
[line ringing]

461
00:27:21,639 --> 00:27:24,059
Madam, your daughter just left.

462
00:27:25,226 --> 00:27:26,978
I told her exactly what you said.

463
00:27:28,605 --> 00:27:30,523
Yes, Madam. I'll be there.

464
00:27:38,365 --> 00:27:40,033
[upbeat music playing]

465
00:27:41,534 --> 00:27:42,410
Madam.

466
00:27:45,246 --> 00:27:46,623
You have a new mission.

467
00:27:48,291 --> 00:27:51,252
You have been trained
to be my best fighter.

468
00:27:51,753 --> 00:27:55,507
And now is your chance
to display your skill.

469
00:28:01,221 --> 00:28:03,181
Kill Lily Cruz.

470
00:28:04,224 --> 00:28:07,852
But, Madam, Lily Cruz knows
you are Red Dragon.

471
00:28:08,686 --> 00:28:11,564
For all we know, she's already
working on an exposé.

472
00:28:12,899 --> 00:28:14,818
How will we get rid of her

473
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:17,612
when we know
she's also plotting against us?

474
00:28:18,488 --> 00:28:19,656
Relax.

475
00:28:20,073 --> 00:28:22,951
You're the soldier, and I'm the brains.

476
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:27,872
Until the last drop of her blood spills…

477
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:32,210
until she draws her last breath…

478
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:35,088
I'll plan her demise.

479
00:28:35,713 --> 00:28:39,551
I just need for you
to execute the perfect crime.

480
00:28:42,595 --> 00:28:45,849
I want you to kill Lily Cruz.

481
00:28:46,391 --> 00:28:49,602
[ominous music playing]

482
00:29:10,290 --> 00:29:12,292
[unsettling music swelling]

483
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:22,051
[unsettling music playing]

484
00:30:01,508 --> 00:30:04,302
[unsettling music continues]

485
00:30:08,306 --> 00:30:10,016
[thumping]

486
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:36,835
[tense music playing]

487
00:31:04,028 --> 00:31:07,240
[tense music continues]

488
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:41,524
Lily Cruz. Lily Cruz. Lily--
Who are you really?

489
00:31:42,942 --> 00:31:45,445
I don't understand. I haven't met you,

490
00:31:45,528 --> 00:31:47,113
but I can't stop myself
from thinking about you.

491
00:31:47,196 --> 00:31:48,197
I always see you…

492
00:31:48,698 --> 00:31:50,074
in my dreams.

493
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:51,951
I don't understand what's happening.

494
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:55,246
Why do I feel like
I've known you for a long time?

495
00:31:56,331 --> 00:31:58,791
Why do I feel this way for you?

496
00:32:04,172 --> 00:32:05,173
I'm so confused.

497
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:12,263
Why does it feel like
I'm in love with you?

498
00:32:27,737 --> 00:32:31,074
Doc, how are Miss Loring and Mr. Pandoy?

499
00:32:32,158 --> 00:32:34,410
How are they doing?

500
00:32:35,912 --> 00:32:36,996
I regret to inform you…

501
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:38,581
they didn't make it.

502
00:32:39,207 --> 00:32:41,042
They were brought to the morgue.

503
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:42,961
Excuse me.

504
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:47,173
[somber music playing]

505
00:33:11,864 --> 00:33:13,658
Mom, where's-- Where's Diego?

506
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:16,202
Where did Diego go?

507
00:33:16,452 --> 00:33:17,453
Where--

508
00:33:17,745 --> 00:33:19,497
Where could he have gone?

509
00:33:20,581 --> 00:33:21,582
[exhales]

510
00:33:34,053 --> 00:33:35,763
Wait, I think I know.

511
00:33:44,772 --> 00:33:46,107
Where's Julio Ardiente?

512
00:33:47,442 --> 00:33:48,735
I need to talk to him.

513
00:33:51,779 --> 00:33:52,864
Let me in.

514
00:33:54,157 --> 00:33:55,241
I'm sorry. We can't do that.

515
00:33:56,409 --> 00:33:57,452
Let me in.

516
00:33:57,535 --> 00:34:00,288
I need to talk to him. He called for me.

517
00:34:14,927 --> 00:34:16,679
-Sir! Sir!
-Julio!

518
00:34:16,763 --> 00:34:17,972
Sir! Sir, wait.

519
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:20,475
[Diego] Julio Ardiente! Julio!

520
00:34:20,558 --> 00:34:21,809
[guard] Sir! Sir, wait.

521
00:34:21,893 --> 00:34:24,979
Julio Ardiente! Come out…

522
00:34:29,859 --> 00:34:30,693
[Diego] Julio!

523
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:32,028
[guard] Sir! Sir, wait.

524
00:34:32,111 --> 00:34:34,614
[Diego] Julio Ardiente! Come out!

525
00:34:34,697 --> 00:34:36,449
-Face me!
-Sir! Sir! Calm down, sir!

526
00:34:36,532 --> 00:34:37,658
-[Lily] Diego!
-I'm here!

527
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:39,702
-Diego!
-Show yourself!

528
00:34:39,786 --> 00:34:40,787
-Come out!
-Diego!

529
00:34:40,870 --> 00:34:42,872
-[guard] Sir! Sir!
-Come out and face me, you bastard!

530
00:34:42,955 --> 00:34:44,999
Let go of him! I said let go of him!

531
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,876
-Diego. Diego.
-Diego, that's enough.

532
00:34:47,919 --> 00:34:48,878
[Jose] Sir!

533
00:34:48,961 --> 00:34:51,005
Let me shut that clucking hen up.

534
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:52,423
[Julio laughing]

535
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:55,384
Who are you calling a clucking hen?

536
00:34:56,511 --> 00:34:58,805
Look! Look at him. Look at that kid.

537
00:34:59,263 --> 00:35:01,432
He's fuming with rage,

538
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:05,603
like a fierce rooster in a cockfight,

539
00:35:05,686 --> 00:35:08,189
waiting to be unleashed,

540
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:11,734
ready to kill anything in its way.

541
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:13,444
Diego, what are you doing here?

542
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:14,904
You're putting yourself in danger.

543
00:35:14,987 --> 00:35:17,907
-I know what I'm doing!
-No. No, you don't.

544
00:35:17,990 --> 00:35:20,243
What you're doing now
won't do you any good.

545
00:35:20,326 --> 00:35:21,994
-Come on. Let's go home.
-Then what?!

546
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:23,621
Tell me, how should I feel…

547
00:35:24,539 --> 00:35:26,749
when they killed my foster parents?!

548
00:35:26,833 --> 00:35:27,583
I know.

549
00:35:27,667 --> 00:35:32,338
Julio Ardiente's life won't be enough
to pay for everything he's done!

550
00:35:32,421 --> 00:35:34,257
-Diego, I know. Diego!
-Hold on!

551
00:35:34,340 --> 00:35:35,466
-Diego!
-Diego!

552
00:35:35,550 --> 00:35:36,968
-Follow him!
-Diego!

553
00:35:37,802 --> 00:35:38,803
You.

554
00:35:39,887 --> 00:35:41,180
You are the clucking hen

555
00:35:41,264 --> 00:35:45,268
because you can't even silence
that rooster out there.

556
00:35:45,351 --> 00:35:46,769
-[Julio scoffs]
-Governor!

557
00:35:47,353 --> 00:35:49,230
Give me this one.

558
00:35:49,313 --> 00:35:51,566
I'll show you who's going
to be the last man standing.

559
00:35:52,733 --> 00:35:54,360
Last man standing?

560
00:35:55,820 --> 00:35:57,113
You're like a parrot…

561
00:35:57,738 --> 00:35:58,948
that won't shut up.

562
00:36:00,449 --> 00:36:03,202
Change of plans.

563
00:36:03,703 --> 00:36:04,954
Use your head!

564
00:36:05,329 --> 00:36:07,915
Do you want me to be suspended again

565
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:09,876
before I even get back to the capitol?

566
00:36:09,959 --> 00:36:12,545
Governor, this is the perfect
time to get rid of that pest.

567
00:36:12,628 --> 00:36:14,463
He might be a pest.

568
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:18,092
But we're going to do it right this time.

569
00:36:19,594 --> 00:36:21,095
I have a better plan.

570
00:36:23,055 --> 00:36:25,099
This is going to work.

571
00:36:25,474 --> 00:36:27,476
[Julio laughing]

572
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:32,481
This will be fun.

573
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:34,025
[Julio chuckles]

574
00:36:34,942 --> 00:36:35,943
[Lily] Diego.

575
00:36:36,152 --> 00:36:37,945
[tense music playing]

576
00:36:38,654 --> 00:36:40,281
-[Jepoy] Diego.
-[Lily] Hey!

577
00:36:40,781 --> 00:36:41,908
-Jepoy.
-Diego.

578
00:36:42,491 --> 00:36:44,744
-[Lily] Let go… Let go of him.
-[Jepoy] Let go of him.

579
00:36:45,494 --> 00:36:46,495
Diego.

580
00:36:48,581 --> 00:36:52,543
[tense music continues playing]

581
00:36:53,794 --> 00:36:57,882
[Julio clapping]

582
00:37:00,384 --> 00:37:01,385
My!

583
00:37:02,428 --> 00:37:04,972
Your performance is what…

584
00:37:05,848 --> 00:37:09,268
people of my age would call "fiery,"

585
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:11,062
or…

586
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:13,773
people of your age would call…

587
00:37:14,815 --> 00:37:15,733
"lit."

588
00:37:16,442 --> 00:37:17,610
You bastard!

589
00:37:18,861 --> 00:37:21,739
Why did you drag them into this?
They were innocent!

590
00:37:24,492 --> 00:37:25,576
Diego, you're…

591
00:37:26,661 --> 00:37:28,788
making up things out of…

592
00:37:30,206 --> 00:37:31,207
thin air.

593
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:32,917
You know what?

594
00:37:33,542 --> 00:37:36,671
Try backing up
your accusations with the truth.

595
00:37:37,505 --> 00:37:38,923
Because if you can't do that…

596
00:37:41,300 --> 00:37:44,971
you're nothing but a street magician who--

597
00:37:45,054 --> 00:37:46,013
-Diego.
-Diego.

598
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:48,057
-Diego.
-You bastard!

599
00:37:48,808 --> 00:37:49,600
Diego!

600
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:52,228
-You bastard!
-Diego!

601
00:37:52,812 --> 00:37:54,480
I'll kill you!

602
00:37:55,064 --> 00:37:56,691
-You bastard!
-No, don't!

603
00:37:56,774 --> 00:37:57,858
-Papa!
-Jepoy!

604
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:00,486
-Hey! Get out…
-Diego!

605
00:38:00,569 --> 00:38:01,988
[Diego growls]

606
00:38:02,071 --> 00:38:02,863
[Julio coughing]

607
00:38:02,947 --> 00:38:04,365
You monster!

608
00:38:04,448 --> 00:38:05,491
[Emilia shrieking]

609
00:38:05,574 --> 00:38:06,492
Stop it!

610
00:38:06,575 --> 00:38:07,660
You bastard!

611
00:38:08,369 --> 00:38:09,203
-Hey!
-You…

612
00:38:09,287 --> 00:38:11,706
-Diego.
-Oh my God. Papa!

613
00:38:11,789 --> 00:38:13,416
Diego. Diego.

614
00:38:15,084 --> 00:38:17,044
Get out, you bastard!

615
00:38:18,087 --> 00:38:19,880
[Emilia] You're all trespassing!

616
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,048
[Julio coughing]

617
00:38:22,049 --> 00:38:24,010
Take him to jail!

618
00:38:24,635 --> 00:38:26,012
You saw what he did!

619
00:38:26,637 --> 00:38:29,265
He was going to kill me in my own house.

620
00:38:30,057 --> 00:38:31,684
[Julio coughing]

621
00:38:31,767 --> 00:38:35,688
What are you waiting for?!
Take him outside! Do it, now!

622
00:38:36,355 --> 00:38:37,273
-[Lily] Diego.
-[Emilia] Well?!

623
00:38:37,356 --> 00:38:38,232
[Raul] Hold on. What's this?

624
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:40,985
-I'll kill you!
-Hey! Hey! Hey! Wait!

625
00:38:41,068 --> 00:38:43,571
Let go of my son! What is this, huh?

626
00:38:44,363 --> 00:38:46,741
Why are you doing this to my son?
He didn't do anything.

627
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:49,660
Shut it, Raul! I saw it with my two eyes!

628
00:38:49,744 --> 00:38:51,746
He pushed Papa! I saw it!

629
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:53,622
[Lily] Do you know why he did that?

630
00:38:55,124 --> 00:38:57,335
It's only because your father

631
00:38:57,418 --> 00:38:59,962
had Miss Loring and Mr. Pandoy killed.

632
00:39:00,046 --> 00:39:02,423
[tense music swells]

633
00:39:03,215 --> 00:39:04,508
Papa, is this true?

634
00:39:09,513 --> 00:39:11,307
-No.
-Liar!

635
00:39:13,517 --> 00:39:14,852
Whatever that is, stop it!

636
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:17,104
Don't ever hurt my son, Emilia!

637
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:19,774
-Fine, then!
-[Emilia] Get out of here!

638
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:22,610
Then go with your son!
Take them both to jail!

639
00:39:22,693 --> 00:39:24,612
-You should be the one in jail!
-Blah!

640
00:39:24,695 --> 00:39:28,324
Blah! Blah! Blah! Blah!
Take those savages away!

641
00:39:28,407 --> 00:39:29,283
Yeah, get out!

642
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:31,619
I promise you this, Julio Ardiente…

643
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:37,583
[Diego] You'll pay for what
you did to my foster parents!

644
00:39:38,125 --> 00:39:39,126
[scoffs]

645
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:40,836
I'll bring you down!

646
00:39:41,504 --> 00:39:43,172
I'll bring you down!

647
00:39:43,255 --> 00:39:44,548
-That's enough. That's enough!
-Take him to jail!

648
00:39:44,632 --> 00:39:45,758
-Enough!
-Take him to jail!

649
00:39:51,972 --> 00:39:53,599
Now, Ardientes.

650
00:39:54,225 --> 00:39:55,309
See?

651
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:57,645
See, Julio Ardiente?

652
00:39:58,437 --> 00:40:03,401
With every person you hurt,
fate itself will drag you down.

653
00:40:05,194 --> 00:40:07,113
No. I didn't kill--

654
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:12,034
Drop the damn act!
Because you can never deceive me.

655
00:40:12,618 --> 00:40:14,787
I know you had them killed!

656
00:40:19,834 --> 00:40:22,128
And because of what you did to Diego,

657
00:40:22,211 --> 00:40:24,713
you just declared another war.

658
00:40:25,589 --> 00:40:26,590
Oh.

659
00:40:32,847 --> 00:40:33,848
The question is…

660
00:40:36,267 --> 00:40:37,768
are you ready for one?

661
00:40:40,187 --> 00:40:43,649
There's only one way for you
to find out, Julio Ardiente.

662
00:40:44,066 --> 00:40:46,694
[tense music swells]

663
00:40:54,076 --> 00:40:55,161
Try me.

664
00:40:58,330 --> 00:40:59,373
Get out…

665
00:41:00,624 --> 00:41:01,542
-of my house.
-And you?

666
00:41:01,625 --> 00:41:02,960
Don't you point at me!

667
00:41:03,043 --> 00:41:04,420
I will point at you--

668
00:41:05,129 --> 00:41:06,130
This is my house!

669
00:41:06,881 --> 00:41:08,674
-You know what?
-[Julio] Enough, enough.

670
00:41:09,049 --> 00:41:11,969
Why don't you visit
your dragon of a mother?

671
00:41:12,428 --> 00:41:15,973
Yes, Emilia, your mother is scared

672
00:41:16,056 --> 00:41:17,683
because I know everything.

673
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:21,437
How Helena Montoya is Red Dragon!

674
00:41:22,021 --> 00:41:23,147
Oh.

675
00:41:23,230 --> 00:41:25,608
I see. But you need to leave our house.

676
00:41:25,691 --> 00:41:27,067
Leave! Get out, all of you!

677
00:41:27,526 --> 00:41:29,236
-Now!
-We will!

678
00:41:29,653 --> 00:41:30,779
You don't have to repeat yourself.

679
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:33,782
We wouldn't want to stay in a
house full of murderers, anyway!

680
00:41:33,866 --> 00:41:34,742
[Julio] Typical…

681
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:36,660
Why are you still here?! Get out! Now!

682
00:41:36,744 --> 00:41:37,620
-We're leaving!
-[Julio] It's enough!

683
00:41:37,703 --> 00:41:38,787
-Right now!
-[Julio] It is enough!

684
00:41:38,871 --> 00:41:40,331
-Now!
-It is enough, Emilia!

685
00:41:40,414 --> 00:41:41,624
It is all right.

686
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:43,542
-What?
-Leave them be. Leave them be.

687
00:41:43,626 --> 00:41:44,793
Leave now!

688
00:41:44,877 --> 00:41:46,962
[tense music playing]

689
00:41:56,722 --> 00:41:59,058
Hey, officers! Don't just stand there!

690
00:41:59,141 --> 00:42:01,602
Get rid of these trespassers!

691
00:42:02,853 --> 00:42:03,854
[Raul] We're leaving.

692
00:42:03,938 --> 00:42:04,939
[Emilia scoffs]

693
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:07,358
Get out!

694
00:42:08,192 --> 00:42:09,568
Get out!

695
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:17,451
What?

696
00:42:19,578 --> 00:42:20,829
You believe them?

697
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:22,498
That I had them killed?

698
00:42:24,959 --> 00:42:26,752
-[Emilia laughing]
-You like it, huh?

699
00:42:26,835 --> 00:42:28,796
-Mm-hm.
-[Julio laughing]

700
00:42:28,879 --> 00:42:29,755
Well done.

701
00:42:30,965 --> 00:42:32,591
-Thank you.
-[laughing]

702
00:42:32,675 --> 00:42:34,885
[Julio] These people never learn.

703
00:42:35,177 --> 00:42:38,097
Never mess with Julio Ardiente…

704
00:42:38,556 --> 00:42:39,890
and Emilia.

705
00:42:40,349 --> 00:42:43,185
[both laughing maniacally]

706
00:42:44,687 --> 00:42:46,188
[both exhale heavily]

707
00:42:48,023 --> 00:42:49,900
I will kill them! I will kill them!

708
00:42:49,984 --> 00:42:51,860
-Diego.
-Just let me do this!

709
00:42:51,944 --> 00:42:53,237
Diego, wait.

710
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:57,366
Listen to me first.

711
00:42:58,659 --> 00:43:00,452
I know how it feels, Diego.

712
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:02,079
I know how much your heart is hurting.

713
00:43:02,162 --> 00:43:03,163
But please.

714
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:04,415
Diego.

715
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:07,126
Diego, don't be so reckless, please.

716
00:43:07,209 --> 00:43:08,877
Don't let your anger get the best of you.

717
00:43:08,961 --> 00:43:10,379
What do you want me to do?

718
00:43:12,339 --> 00:43:14,341
They killed my foster parents.

719
00:43:15,467 --> 00:43:17,970
Of all people, you should
be the one who understands

720
00:43:18,053 --> 00:43:20,055
because you lost your loved ones too.

721
00:43:20,389 --> 00:43:22,808
Your father and Nanny Carlotta
were killed…

722
00:43:23,517 --> 00:43:25,019
all because of them!

723
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:27,313
They need to die.

724
00:43:28,355 --> 00:43:30,232
Yes, you're right, Diego.

725
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:33,485
We both lost our loved ones
all because of the Ardientes.

726
00:43:34,153 --> 00:43:37,489
The pain and anger you feel right now,

727
00:43:37,573 --> 00:43:40,367
I know them well
because they're still in my heart.

728
00:43:42,911 --> 00:43:46,081
But, Diego, you know
that I can't kill anyone!

729
00:43:47,541 --> 00:43:49,126
If you want to seek justice,

730
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:50,878
I'll help you.

731
00:43:50,961 --> 00:43:53,881
In the right way.
My family and I will help you.

732
00:43:53,964 --> 00:43:56,675
I'm the one who lost my foster parents,
so I'll do it my way.

733
00:43:59,428 --> 00:44:00,471
So, please…

734
00:44:01,430 --> 00:44:02,723
Please stay out of it.

735
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:05,142
I can't do that, Diego!

736
00:44:07,978 --> 00:44:10,230
Because I'm scared!

737
00:44:10,314 --> 00:44:12,733
If you could only see yourself right now!

738
00:44:13,275 --> 00:44:16,195
It's like you're ready to kill,
and I won't let you do that!

739
00:44:16,278 --> 00:44:17,905
I won't let you turn into
a criminal, Diego!

740
00:44:17,988 --> 00:44:21,158
But there's no place for justice
here in Ardiente!

741
00:44:22,076 --> 00:44:23,202
You know that!

742
00:44:24,161 --> 00:44:26,121
So, let's stop fooling ourselves.

743
00:44:27,539 --> 00:44:28,999
I will kill them.

744
00:44:29,083 --> 00:44:32,086
-Diego, don't. Please.
-I will kill them!

745
00:44:32,169 --> 00:44:35,047
-Diego. Diego, no. Diego!
-[Jepoy] Diego!

746
00:44:37,007 --> 00:44:37,883
[door closes]

747
00:44:37,966 --> 00:44:41,220
[tense music playing]

748
00:44:56,276 --> 00:44:58,404
[Diego] <i>The old Diego Torillo is gone.</i>

749
00:44:58,487 --> 00:45:03,534
<i>All that's left is a man thirsty</i>
<i>for the blood of his enemies!</i>

750
00:45:03,617 --> 00:45:06,787
[Georgina] <i>We have to secure an advantage</i>
<i>before Julio's camp does.</i>

751
00:45:06,870 --> 00:45:08,789
[Lily] <i>And the evidence</i>
<i>against Red Dragon?</i>

752
00:45:08,872 --> 00:45:10,833
<i>All pieces of evidence</i>
<i>are admissible in court.</i>

753
00:45:10,916 --> 00:45:11,834
<i>We need a…</i>

754
00:45:11,917 --> 00:45:14,503
<i>A credible witness. I know someone.</i>

755
00:45:14,586 --> 00:45:17,798
<i>And I know where to find her.</i>

756
00:45:17,881 --> 00:45:21,260
<i>That Torillo better be careful.</i>
<i>One wrong move,</i>

757
00:45:21,343 --> 00:45:25,222
<i>and he'll meet his nanny</i>
<i>and uncle in purgatory.</i>

758
00:45:25,305 --> 00:45:28,934
[gunshots]

759
00:45:29,017 --> 00:45:31,145
[theme music playing]
